Object assets in this directory — attribution
=============================================

These 39 files (13 `.urdf`, 13 `.obj`, 13 `sample_points.npy`) are redistributed
from **InterMimic**, byte for byte. They are not our files, and they are not
OMOMO's original mesh files either: the `.obj` are trimesh re-exports produced by
InterMimic's own asset preparation, and the URDF wrappers and surface samples are
InterMimic's work, not ours.

    InterMimic: Towards Universal Whole-Body Control for Physics-Based
    Human-Object Interactions
    Sirui Xu, Hung Yu Ling, Yu-Xiong Wang, Liang-Yan Gui
    IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2025
    https://github.com/Sirui-Xu/InterMimic

InterMimic is MIT-licensed, which permits this redistribution provided its notice
travels with the files. That notice is reproduced in full below.

The underlying object *geometry* originates with OMOMO, which InterMimic
processed into this form. OMOMO is separately MIT-licensed and is cited below
too. OMOMO ships 15 objects; `mop` and `vacuum` are articulated and are not part
of this release, leaving the 13 the paper evaluates on.

    Object Motion Guided Human Motion Synthesis
    Jiaman Li, Jiajun Wu, C. Karen Liu
    ACM Transactions on Graphics (SIGGRAPH Asia), 2023
    https://github.com/lijiaman/omomo_release

The OMOMO *motion capture* is NOT redistributed here — only the object assets.
